Q1. Animal Sound

You are developing an application for a zoo. Every animal has a sound() behavior. The Animal class provides a general sound, but the Dog class provides its own sound.

class Animal {
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal sound");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    @Override
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}

The following code is executed:

Animal a = new Dog();
a.sound();

What will be printed?

A. Animal sound
B. Dog barks
C. Compilation error
D. Nothing

